\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Components of a substation connected in series. The power produced by the wind turbines flows through every component before reaching the onshore grid, and each component can only carry the fraction $1 - \ell _m$ of the full power. The power transmitted to the grid (hatched) is thus limited by the most degraded component, here component $2$, and is $\min _m (1 - \ell _m) = 1 - \max _m \ell _m = 0.7$. The capacity loss of the substation is $\max _m \ell _m = 0.3$, and not the sum $0.4$ of the capacity losses.}}{8}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:series}{{2}{8}{Components of a substation connected in series. The power produced by the wind turbines flows through every component before reaching the onshore grid, and each component can only carry the fraction $1 - \ell _m$ of the full power. The power transmitted to the grid (hatched) is thus limited by the most degraded component, here component $2$, and is $\min _m (1 - \ell _m) = 1 - \max _m \ell _m = 0.7$. The capacity loss of the substation is $\max _m \ell _m = 0.3$, and not the sum $0.4$ of the capacity losses}{figure.caption.11}{}}
